Saved by the Eggs!
-or-
How many pets does it take to ascend?

Questis-val-hum-law-fem.  This is at least my 50th or so incarnation of
Questis, I stopped counting above 25 (that doesn't include all the Sandra's,
Jane's, and such, who were also val-hum-law-fem's)

This was the first one to make it.  Herein lies a long tale of Questis's
journey through the dungeons of doom, ultimately to become the first ever of
her kind to make it out alive.

It started simply enough.  Fought a few enemies, found some decent
equipment.  One sweet find was a +4 orcish helm on level 2 or 3, that kept
my AC low for quite a while.  I found an early pair of magic lamps while
working through the mines.  I entered the mall, and, of course, the altar
was cross-aligned.  Darn.  So I continued downward, reaching the bottom of
the mine, it was the one with all the mimics and such, and as I searched for
the luckstone, I acquired a few more pets.  So now I had Rusty (my original
dog) Morris (a housecat) Snowball (large cat) and Fido (little dog).  By the
time I found the stone and was heading out though, only Snowball, Morris and
Rusty survived.  I walked around minetown, and Snowball attacked the watch
captain, and died.  So now I'm down to two pets.  I used my first wish for
+3 SDSM, and my second wish for a +3 CoMR (fireproof of course).  I
continued back into the main part of the mines, and ran into a wraith.  I
killed the wraith, it left a corpse, but before I could reach it, rusty ate
it and turned into a Vampire! (turns out it was a chameleon corpse).  So I
renamed him to something more appropriate, so now I have a large cat named
Morris, and a Vampire named Nosferatu.  I asked for some advice, and then
headed to minetown with a new purpose: Nosferatu would win me a silver
saber.  I walked stealthily up to the watch captain, zapped him with a wand
of sleep (mistake, he's sleep resistance) and then hit him with a potion of
paralysis.  We both were caught in it, so I watched, frozen to the floor, as
Nosferatu killed the watch captain.  He became a Vampire Lord! While I took
the silver saber, Nosferatu killed every living thing in minetown, clearing
out the altar so I could convert it.  ~10 sacrifices later, I'm the proud
owner of Mojo!

Fast forward a bit, Sokobon had a BoH, which was excellent.  Nothing could
really stand against me.  And Nosferatu was indestructible.  I killed and
ate a couple tengu's, gaining teleport control on the second, and then ran
into an energy vortex.  This was one of my closest calls ever.  I'm inside
the vortex, with no shock resistance, trying in vain to beat it to death.  I
look down and notice that my hp is only 1.  Said a prayer, and then fought
my way out, with 20 health to spare.  Headed back, found a altar, and did
some sacrificing, waiting for something I could get shock resistance from
would show up.  Said some prayers when I could on the altar, and wouldn't
you know, I got crowned.  Well, at least I have shock resistance!

Moved on down, let a priest of Odin have some of my gold, got some
protection.  Walked around a little bit, and then fell through a trapdoor
that left me several levels below where I was before.  Right next to a
Master Mind Flayer.  The fight was quick, I got my brain eaten once or
twice, but I emerged victorious.  Headed back up to where Nosferatu was
waiting for me (Morris was dead by now :(.  So I had a brilliant idea, I'll
quaff a sink till potions come out, then I'll be able to remember them.
Took off the CoMR, quaffed till I was a dragon, continued on, and...

Your turn into a forest centaur.  You break out of your armor

That was a setback.  While in dragon form, I laid a couple eggs, which
hatched into twin baby silver dragons, Hack and Slash.  I decided to try to
level them up, figuring that if I couldn't have reflection, at least my pets
should.  Hack died early on, sadly.  I found my quest, turned out to be on
the rogue level, and went to see Lord Surtur.  This was the first time I'd
been on the quest with controlled teleportits (the other two times I made it
this far I didn't have control).  Quest was relatively easy, but I then
realized what reflection was good for:

Lord Surtur zaps a wand of lightning.  The bolt of lightning hits you.  Your
ring of slow digestion explodes! Your ring of free action explodes! ....
etc. for about 1/2 of my wands.

Well, that was a setback, after getting the orb of fate I checked some
earlier levels, and found a spare =oFA I had dropped earlier.  I found an
amulet that turned out to be magical breathing, the first time I'd ever had
such a thing.  I also found a ring of levitation, which was convenient.
Slash finally leveled up, becoming a full on Silver Dragon.  Slash didn't
seem cool enough a name for such a beast, so his new name became Slasher.
Alas, Slasher got left behind, only to be found later on level 2.  At this
point, he was no longer tame, and Nosferatu killed him.  He left scales! I
named them "Slasher's Legacy" to reflect their origin, and to always be
reminded of how one of my pets saved me.  I now continued on, with
reflection, MR, decent AC, and Mojo/Silver Saber, so again, nothing was able
to put up much of a fight.  Nosferatu killed the priest of Odin, refunding
me about 30k gold that I then took 3 levels down to the priest of Tyr.  At
this point, my naked AC was something like 1 or 0.

Found Medusa's level, it was the one with several buildings and such.
Nosferatu killed the Titan that started in the first room.  At this point, I
knew I had an insane pet. Nosferatu wasn't afraid of anything, and he could
take nearly anyhting on, never slowing down.  I floated to Medusa, showed
her a shiny new mirror I found, and then headed to the castle, 2 levels
below.  Cleared out the castle with no trouble (went in the back way) and
then grabbed the castle wand.  Filled out my Ascension kit, including

Helm of Telepathy
Gauntlets of Power
Boots of Speed


plus ?oCharging, ?oEnchant weapon (never seen one before) and a couple magic
markers.  Read, wrote, repeated to get all my armor to +4 or 5, and my two
weapons to +6 (took me 3 tries to make the Silver Saber +7, but I eventually
got that).  Now my AC was -40, I found a stethoscope, and turns out
Nosferatu was level 18, AC -19, with 144 HP.  I'd watch him fight, and he
never seemed to take damage.  That was cool.

So I headed into Gehennom, fought around there, killed demon princes like
they were nothing.  Then, I began to get scared.  I remembered my last
character like this, Sandra II, who died due to a double-trouble'd WoY +
Demogorgan, Yeenoghu, and a summon storm of nasties.  So I headed back up,
looking around for a spare /oDeath, or maybe some way to polymorph myself
into a cockatrice...

Read my last scroll of identify, (blessed obviously) and started to identify
rings.  Polymorph.  Second ring: Polymorph control.  Then the scroll ended.
So I put them both on, cockatriced myself, and laid about a 16 eggs.
Polyselfed into human a few times till I liked my level and stats, by then
the eggs were stacking, so it was time to continue.  First though, just for
fun, I ate a spare "oMagical breathing.  Got it as an intrinsic.  SWEET!


Went down to Vlad's, took him out in one or maybe two hits (he's pathetic),
got the "oLS, wore that for a while.  Went all the way to the VS, marked it,
headed back up, looking for the wizard's towers.  Along the way, I found a
figurine of a Sandestin, so I blessed it and got a new pet.  Being a
shapeshifter, I was assured that Odo would die horribly, but I had no
idea....  See, when I found the fake tower, he turned into a gremlin, and
multiplied.  It was INSANE! I had like 20 shapeshifting pets.  However,  I
wonder if the AI got confused, i.e. maybe the shapeshifting clones still
thought they were gremlins?  See, what happened was, all of the Odo's save
the original jumped back in the moat, most of which drowned immediately, the
rest polymorphing and dying.  Odo died a little later, while in the form of
a mold or something like that.  So I go up to the WoY tower, then chicken
out, and head back out.  I was going to go drop a bunch of spare stuff in my
stash, get rid of unneeded stuff, etc.  I blew my magic whistle, and my pet
green mold named Nosferatu showed up.   Great, just great, and I thought I
was going to ascend with him.... So I pushed him into the polytrap a few
times, eventually turning him into an orc zombie, who was killed quickly by
a random enemy.  So much for pets, or so I thought.  In the treasure zoo of
the Wizard's Tower, I saw a vampire lord, so I tamed him with my recently
polypiled magic harp.  In the process, I also got a vampire and a fire
vortex.  All three met their ends in the treasure zoo, the fire vortex
lasting the longest.  Found a figurine of a chameleon, blessed it, applied
it, and it became a hostile iron golem.  Well, fine, forget pets.


So I ran up to the WoY, knocked a hole in the wall, and threw an egg at him.
Grabbed the book, invoked the Orb of Fate, and then ran to the VS.  Entered
Moloch's Sanctum, where the Wizard once again greeted me.  He cast double
trouble, then entered the temple to battle the high priest.  I walked
around, found the door, and watched from one end of the room as the two
wizards attacked the priest.  One got to close to me, so I egged him, then
decided that it was getting too dangerous in here, and egged the other two
Grabbed the AoY, and quaffed a cursed !oGL.  The run out wasn't too
impressive, I just read every ?oTeleport I had and used ^T when I could, the
evil force kicked in and I had to run through level 41 at least 3 or 4 times
(annoying, because the stairs were far and it was a no teleport level).  The
AoY didn't start blocking my teleportation till I was about on level 20 of
the dungeon, where at one point it blocked a couple scrolls and three ^T in
a row.

Earth wasn't so bad, Egged the Wizard once again, used my wands of digging,
then realized that I had no ?oGold detection, and my orb of fate only had 3
charges left... So I wandered around for a while, gave in and used the Orb
of fate.  Used it again on Air, where it seemed that the air elementals were
harder than usual (usually I'd kill them before they could engulf me)
Rodney showed up again, only to find himself with egg on his face.  Used my
last orb of fate charge on fire, and then swam around water for a little
bit.  I suddenly had a flash of inspiration: I had an unidentified scroll,
and I had never seen (or remembered perhaps) gold detection.  So I confused
myself, read it, and, guess what, I was right.  It was gold detection.  Ran
to the portal.  Arrived on Astral, dropped some wands, and made a dash to
the right.  Ran into famine, who was a pushover, so I pushed him over and
ran on by.  The insects got really annoying, but nothing was hurting me.  I
walked toward a temple, and saw a "renegade priest of Tyr".  I assumed that
this couldn't be my temple, why would a priest be a renegade in his own
temple? I went in anyway, and wouldn't you know it, I'm greeted by the High
Priest of Tyr.

What do you want to sacrifice? [hBV or ?*]?
You offer the Amulet of Yendor to Tyr... An invisible choir sings, and you
are bathed in radiance... The voice of Tyr rings out: "Congratulations,
mortal!" "In return for thy service, I grant thee the gift of immortality!"
You ascend to the status of Demigoddess...

